== Trivia ==
* Keeper was publicly revealed to players through an [http://imgur.com/V2l5TaN alternate reality game] created by the developers; however, files alluding to Keeper's existence already were found after the initial release of ''Afterbirth''. With the conclusion of the [[Keeper_ARG|ARG]], a patch was released to fully add Keeper to the game as a playable character.
* {{dlc|nr}} In the game's files, there is a character called "[[Cut Content#Old Man Keeper|Old Man Keeper]]", which was most likely meant to be the 2nd ''Afterbirth'' character instead of Keeper. However, he was replaced with this Keeper. This sprite is used for April Fool's Day's daily run since 2016, as Keeper's sprite is changed to this sprite for the day.
* Keeper's starting health is listed as "II" on the character selection screen, despite having no red hearts. This is unique among such characters, whose health is usually listed as "-I" or "?".
** {{dlc|r}} The starting health will become "III" after defeating {{E|Hush}} with him.
* The Keeper was created for the sake of being "[https://twitter.com/edmundmcmillen/status/1238378074967699456 another challenge character]" for this game (the other character is {{c|The Lost}}).
* As a secret character, Keeper does not appear on the character select screen until unlocked.
** He shares this trait with {{C|???}}, {{C|The Lost}}, and {{C|The Forgotten|a+}}.
* Edmund has confirmed that Keeper (and by extension, {{E|Shopkeeper}}s) is a mummified version of Isaac from previous runs.<ref>https://twitter.com/edmundmcmillen/status/1568484195252731904</ref>

